title Copal fruit fourth read: no unrostered witness, no build
prompt Run the copal baton lap: read the inner prompt and the card, take the ruled fruit (one unrostered chapter witness), claim it, roster it, prove it from both sides, and log.
think The ruled fruit is one unrostered witness under tools/gen/chapter/. I checked the room two ways: a loose check that greps the roster for each file's basename, and a strict check that requires a real path line naming each file.
think The loose check flagged brush_parse_tame_density.sh and prin_ticker.rish. The strict check added fascia_metric_v0.rish, plus several .brix and README files that are data or prose, not witnesses.
think brush_parse_tame_density.sh is rostered on purpose: its guard row points at brush_parse_density_witness.rish, whose control plants 19, 20 and 25 markers. Its roster comment says the control is the guard.
think prin_ticker.rish is a thin hand. Its witness, prin_ticker_witness.rish, has its own roster row. fascia_metric_v0.rish is an elder shim whose roster row points at the living runner, fascia_metric.rish.
think So no witness in the room lacks coverage. A new roster row for any of these would duplicate a guard that already runs, which is a cost with no witness behind it.
think The card also parks the remaining unrostered chapter witnesses as Keaton's word. A fourth read reaching the same answer means the fruit is spent, and I would not invent a row to make it look live.
obs No claim was opened and no roster row was added. A claim commits a board row for a file no peer can be reading, so claiming nothing is the honest move here.
obs The claim check at the start of the lap read clear: zero live claims, commits_behind=3 against xy. The nib witness read the card stale at HEAD 3a7152e182, so the card's Git nib is carried forward in this same commit.
rota lap 13381, row 1 -- air feels: the row asks what can be felt in the room's own shape. I read the fruit, the roster, and the card, and did not deep-read the council row in full this lap.
orbit round 1 Aries -- Commence. Finish one to-do. The to-do this lap was to finish the fruit's question, and the answer was that nothing in the room is left unrostered.
scope log-only lap: this session log and its day-shelf row, with the card's Git nib carried to HEAD. Runs read-only checks; changes no code, roster, or witness.
status GREEN on the read-only checks: the fleet claim scan read clear, and the strict path check found no unrostered witness. No build, no roster row, no push. The fruit is spent until Keaton's word names a chapter witness to roster.
file construction/ITINERARY.md why the Git nib moves to HEAD 3a7152e182 so the follow-up does not read stale
